{# PROPOSAL -- for C1 to place in templates/macros. NOT active. NOT loaded by any render harness. #}
{# audit_ref: codex-manager-current-source-audits-20260923-0315 (F_representation_audit item 5) #}
{# target: LICENSE #}
{# tested: false (body decomposition into declared section kinds is OPEN; C1 wires + byte-parity verifies) #}
{#
   REPLACES the disallowed escape hatch. LICENSE.j2 today concatenates whole component
   bodies by hardcoded index (components[0..2].body). A loop over whole bodies
     {% for s in sections %}{{ s.body }}{% endfor %}
   is the SAME escape hatch and is ALSO disallowed. So is a loop where each section carries
   its OWN indent/separator (per-instance literal paste, which collapses to whole-body).

   This macro takes a DECLARED ordered section list plus a PER-KIND format map. Each section
   carries only {kind, text}; indent / terminator / separator are looked up by KIND from
   `formats`, which is sourced from the schema (license_section_formats.<kind>.*).

   OPEN: decomposing the three component bodies (CISA preamble, CC0-1.0, Apache-2.0) into
   declared section kinds (title_block | heading | numbered_clause | enumerated_item |
   paragraph) is NOT done. Until it is, this target stays a violation and tested:false.

   params -> declared schema keys (emitted-structural-literals-schema.yaml):
     sections -> license_sections[] (ordered; each {kind, text}; data)
     formats  -> license_section_formats.<kind>.{indent,terminator,separator} (renderable-OPEN)
   No parameter has a default; no string/number literal appears in the body.
   Terminal newline is OWNED by this macro via the last section's terminator.
#}
{% macro render_license_sections(sections, formats) -%}
{% for s in sections -%}
{% set fmt = formats[s.kind] -%}
{{ fmt.indent }}{{ s.text }}{{ fmt.terminator }}{{ fmt.separator }}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- endmacro %}
